**1. An information processing system for controlling operation of a mobile object, the information processing system comprising:**

an integrated circuit (IC) tag associated with the mobile object and storing tag information including at least an identifier of the mobile object;

a mobile terminal comprising an IC-tag reader, a user interface, a communication interface, and one or more processors configured to:  
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;read the tag information from the IC tag;  
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;obtain pilot identification information identifying a person requesting to operate the mobile object; and  
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;transmit, to a server, a verification request including the pilot identification information and the tag information;

the server comprising one or more processors configured to:  
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;obtain, based on the pilot identification information, license information indicating a validity and an authorized operating scope of a pilot license associated with the person;  
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;obtain, based on the identifier of the mobile object, vehicle data indicating at least a type or an operating condition of the mobile object;  
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;determine whether the pilot license is valid for operation of the mobile object by comparing the authorized operating scope with the vehicle data;  
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;generate operation-control information specifying permission or a restriction for operation of the mobile object based on the determination; and  
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;transmit the operation-control information to at least one of the mobile terminal or the mobile object; and

an operation-control device associated with the mobile object and configured, in accordance with the operation-control information, to permit operation of the mobile object when the pilot license is determined to be valid for the mobile object and to prevent or restrict operation of the mobile object when the pilot license is determined not to be valid for the mobile object.

### Exemplary System Description

A system for controlling operation of an unmanned aerial vehicle, the system comprising:

1. an unmanned aerial vehicle including:
   - a flight-control subsystem configured to selectively permit or inhibit operation of the unmanned aerial vehicle; and
   - a communication interface configured to provide vehicle-identification data associated with the unmanned aerial vehicle;

2. a mobile computing device comprising:
   - a wireless communication interface configured to receive the vehicle-identification data from the unmanned aerial vehicle;
   - a memory storing, or configured to receive, operator-license data associated with an operator of the unmanned aerial vehicle;
   - a network interface configured to transmit, to a remote server, an authorization request comprising the vehicle-identification data and the operator-license data; and
   - a processor configured to receive, from the remote server, an authorization determination generated based at least in part on the vehicle-identification data and the operator-license data, and to communicate a control instruction to the unmanned aerial vehicle according to the authorization determination; and

3. the remote server comprising:
   - one or more processors; and
   - a non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the remote server to:
     - receive the authorization request from the mobile computing device;
     - evaluate the vehicle-identification data and the operator-license data against one or more authorization criteria;
     - generate the authorization determination indicating whether operation of the unmanned aerial vehicle is authorized; and
     - transmit the authorization determination to the mobile computing device,

wherein the flight-control subsystem is configured, responsive to the control instruction, to enable operation of the unmanned aerial vehicle when the authorization determination indicates that operation is authorized and to disable or restrict operation of the unmanned aerial vehicle when the authorization determination indicates that operation is not authorized.

### Exemplary Method Claim

A computer-implemented method for controlling an unmanned aerial vehicle, the method comprising:

- receiving, by a mobile computing device and from the unmanned aerial vehicle, vehicle data identifying or characterizing the unmanned aerial vehicle;
- obtaining, by the mobile computing device, operator-license data associated with an operator;
- transmitting, by the mobile computing device to a remote server, the vehicle data and the operator-license data;
- determining, by the remote server, whether operation of the unmanned aerial vehicle is authorized based on at least the vehicle data and the operator-license data;
- transmitting, by the remote server to the mobile computing device, an authorization response representing the determination; and
- causing, by the mobile computing device, the unmanned aerial vehicle to enter:
  - an enabled operational state when the authorization response indicates authorization; or
  - a disabled or operationally restricted state when the authorization response indicates a lack of authorization.

In certain embodiments, the authorization criteria further include license validity, operator qualification, vehicle registration status, geographic restrictions, temporal restrictions, airspace restrictions, insurance status, maintenance status, or combinations thereof.
